      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T22:01:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The TCPM code has logic to track how long the power button is held down and only takes action on the [button release](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c;l\u003d598;drc\u003db168742832ac0a884842f72e70b22b774d711ed4) once the power button duration is known.\n\nDo we need similar support here?  Specifically actions to power down the AP on a long press?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1701,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1701,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "da137858360268e94e1f2578bf9a0779de069198",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b271094b_be900110",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1701,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T00:46:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a preferable implementation compared to the TCPMv2 versions. Adding support for shutdown on long button presses requires us to wait for a button release. This makes the device noticeably slower to process PD power button presses. Just sending a short press when a press event is received gives the following behavior.\n\nS0: show power UI\nSuspned: wake from suspend\nShutdown: boot\n\nI think this is appropriate behavior for a button on a dock. It is similar to how we treat the keyboard \"lock\" key. The internal \"lock\" key needs to be held down to lock the device. We don\u0027t trust that we will get a release event from external lock keys, so those just need to be tapped to lock a chromebook.\n\nI\u0027ve asked whether shutting down is a requirement on b/427360158.",
      "parentUuid": "d3fe7683_2582715a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1701,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1701,
        "endChar": 44
